Z||000007||Zorba||10-17-2000||02:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>Depends on your choich of year and type of V8 engine. But 5K sounds about right for the average swap.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It all depends on whether you buy your conversion kit new, used or unused. The engine you buy. You could start out with a cheap stock sbc v8. One that runs well should not cost you more than $300-$400 if your shop around or pull it off another car.<BR>Later on you can intall a fancy TPI, 383, 400hp 350 crate engine, etc. but even a bone stock V8 will put a smile on your face in comparison to a stock inline 4 or V-6, anyday, anytime. Once you've put all this together, disassembly is actually very simple and you can replaced the old engine with a fresh crate motor. By my logic, you should be able to do everything under $3,000, less if you get your engine with all the peripherals already installed such as distributor, carb, spark plugs,wires,lines, etc. If you want everything new...yeah, it will cost you an arm and a leg. Sometimes, it's worth it to wait around and shop for a v8 fiero, already done. Plan on $5,000-$8,000 for that. More if it is TPI or High PErformance.<P>||||reg||1
